	(title_block
		(title "VMT 04/16 controller - Specimen Protection")
		(date "2026-11-03")
		(rev "0.1")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "Specimen Protection\nSocket for the original 3N2 card (LP 77-070-8, 8-pin edge connector) - kept unchanged.\nSupply 24 V~ (4L1/4L2). t> pot R1 (1 k, MUP 4000) on the front plate. Own Pt100 B3.\n3N2 relay contact 3K3 sits in the SPEC_TRIP loop -> fault relay 2K8 in Fault_Logic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b886b114-6e6f-410f-a8f7-6f949f068915")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- Socket for the original 3N2 card (LP 77-070-8), same pinout as old PL2 (manual p. 58):\n  1 = E/S (pot R1), 8 = A+, 2/3 = Pt100 B3, 4/5 = 24 V~ (4L1/4L2), 6/7 = relay contact 3K3.\n- Card guides so the card is held like on the old PL2.\n- Connector to the t> potentiometer R1 on the front plate (reuse the original pot). Terminals I/II only on ranges below 0 °C - check which 3N2 variant is fitted (0-100 or 0-200 °C).\n- R5 1.5k as in the original circuit (p. 58).\n- SPEC_TRIP_OUT -> 3K3 -> SPEC_TRIP_RET: contact in the loop of fault relay 2K8 (Fault_Logic).\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- Card-edge socket: measure finger count, pitch (likely 3.96 mm) and single/double-sided on the card first, then pick a matching 0.156 in card-edge connector.\n- t> pot: original Megatron MUP 4000, 1 kOhm (reuse). Pot connector: 3-pin JST XH or 3.5 mm terminal block."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 50.8 0)
